# Larger Exterior Book Tabs

Status: DONE
Milestone: M19 Physical edge-attached notebook markers
Dependencies: 19_LIGHTER_PINK_TABS_AND_MATERIAL_STUDY.todo; 23_FULL_WIDTH_AWNING_AND_PLAIN_HERO.todo

## Purpose

The owner clarified that index tabs should be larger, attached at the paper edge,
and project outward. Closed pink covers need text-free varied pastel tabs along
the right edge, rather than only showing flags inside open notebooks.

## Tasks

- [x] Add decorative closed-cover tabs with deterministic varied pastel colours.
- [x] Enlarge real action flags and anchor book-level tabs outside paper edges.
- [x] Reserve sufficient gutters so flags and focus rings are not clipped.
- [x] Preserve full names,48pxtargets, four photos and both-axis viewport fitting.
- [x] Refresh the closed/open notebook README views.
- [x] Run existing fit/site checks and publish with the canopy/hero correction.

## Acceptance criteria

- Preview tabs have no text, controls or accessibility-tree clutter.
- Right-side tabs visibly extend beyond each closed pink cover.
- Open book-level actions attach to an actual paper edge and protrude.
- Pastel variation is stable per notebook, not flickering random runtime state.
- Readable text, keyboard/focus return, direct enquiries and static fallbacks remain.
- No image-tool views, new product facts, weight controls or cream effect.

